# Frozen action data for the 71 restricted-palette repair

`repairCode` is the machine-generated action word for the finite repair
certificate of 71 under the restricted palette.  It is produced from the
checked JSON artifacts `experiments/catalytic_palette_71_witness.json` and
`experiments/catalytic_palette_71_replay.json` and is split into three
consecutive blocks:

* actions `0 .. 1505`    -- build the borrowed word `W` from the seed units
  `U2`, `U8`, `U13` and the 96-node borrow DAG, inside the certificate `x`;
* actions `1506 .. 1774` -- the 269 ordered main schedule actions
  (9 `insert-U8`, 3 `remove-U13`, 3 `reverse-cubic`, 254 oriented `Q` rows);
* actions `1775 .. 3280` -- the formal inverse of the first block, returning
  `W` inside the target certificate `y`.

Each entry is a small `List Nat` decoded by `decodeAct`:
`[a,b,c,d]` is the quadratic replacement `[a,b] -> [c,d]`, `[0,i]` inserts the
`i`-th allowed unit, `[1,i]` removes it, `[2]` is the cubic `C5` and `[3]` its
reverse.  Nothing here is trusted: every entry is re-checked by the executable
interpreter `step`, and every accepted step is turned into an `AllowedMove`.
-/

